description:
Reported on beta: the scores table border looks full white and does not match other components.

ROOT CAUSE, and it is not the table. Tailwind v4 changed the DEFAULT border colour from gray-200 to currentColor. v2/src/styles.css's @layer base block sets box-sizing and body styles but never sets a default border colour, so every bare `border` utility inherits the text colour — near-white on a dark background, near-black on light.

Affected today (bare `border`, no colour class): ui/card.tsx, ui/dialog.tsx, ui/select.tsx (content), ui/badge.tsx, ui/popover.tsx, ui/dropdown-menu.tsx (x2), components/scores-table.tsx.

Not affected: anything passing a colour explicitly — ui/input.tsx and ui/select.tsx's trigger use border-input, board-entry/form.tsx uses border-input, ThemeToggle uses border-line-subtle. That mismatch is exactly why the table reads as "not matching other components": some components name a colour and some rely on a default that no longer exists.

FIX: add the standard shadcn Tailwind-v4 base rule to styles.css so a bare `border` resolves to the design token:

  @layer base {
    * { border-color: var(--color-border); }
  }

One rule fixes the table and every Card, Dialog, Popover, Dropdown and Badge at once. --color-border already maps to --border, which is --border-subtle (#e4e4e7 light / #292929 dark).

Also reported: the border looks DOUBLED between rows. Re-check after the colour fix — a 1px currentColor border is far heavier than the token and may account for the perception. If it survives, suspect the sticky pinned cells interacting with the table's border-collapse.

Found by the owner on beta after the Phase 2 auto-deploy.
